 "segments": [
  {
   "v": "narrator",
   "t": "German finishes his zombie story by imagining himself calmly plating gourmet brain dishes for the undead in the kitchen, leaving Max and the crew deeply unsettled.",
   "gap": 0.8
  },
  {
   "v": "fedya",
   "t": "Братан, ты же меня укусил!",
   "gap": 0.55
  },
  {
   "v": "fedya",
   "t": "Надо было тебя сразу пристрелить.",
   "gap": 0.55
  },
  {
   "v": "german",
   "t": "Вот мозги в красном вине.",
   "gap": 0.55
  },
  {
   "v": "german",
   "t": "И блюдо с кедровыми орешками.",
   "gap": 0.55
  },
  {
   "v": "german",
   "t": "Ещё паштет из гусиных мозгов.",
   "gap": 0.55
  },
  {
   "v": "german",
   "t": "И свежий мозговой коктейль.",
   "gap": 0.55
  },
  {
   "v": "german",
   "t": "Сеня, подай мне большой нож.",
   "gap": 0.55
  },
  {
   "v": "anya",
   "t": "Да, весёлая у вас история.",
   "gap": 0.55
  },
  {
   "v": "anya",
   "t": "Странный у нас коллектив получается.",
   "gap": 0.55
  },
  {
   "v": "fedya",
   "t": "Совсем не смешное кино.",
   "gap": 0.55
  },
  {
   "v": "anya",
   "t": "Давайте лучше дальше кокосы варить.",
   "gap": 0.55
  },
  {
   "v": "german",
   "t": "Работайте, не отвлекайтесь.",
   "gap": 0.9
  },
  {
   "v": "narrator",
   "t": "Let's go through the end of German's story and the cooks' reaction.",
   "gap": 0.4
  },
  {
   "v": "fedya",
   "t": "Братан, ты же меня укусил!",
   "gap": 0.55
  },
  {
   "v": "narrator",
   "t": "'Bro, you just bit me!' Tied-up Senya manages to chomp Fedya's shoulder.",
   "gap": 0.4
  },
  {
   "v": "fedya",
   "t": "Надо было тебя сразу пристрелить.",
   "gap": 0.55
  },
  {
   "v": "narrator",
   "t": "'We should have shot you right away.' Again, 'need' plus neuter past 'was' forms the regretful phrase 'should have'.",
   "gap": 0.4
  },
  {
   "v": "german",
   "t": "Вот мозги в красном вине.",
   "gap": 0.55
  },
  {
   "v": "narrator",
   "t": "'Here are brains in red wine.' In his own story, German thrives during the apocalypse by cooking haute cuisine for zombies.",
   "gap": 0.4
  },
  {
   "v": "german",
   "t": "И блюдо с кедровыми орешками.",
   "gap": 0.55
  },
  {
   "v": "narrator",
   "t": "'And a dish with pine nuts.' In Russian, pine nuts are called 'cedar little nuts' and take the instrumental plural after 'with'.",
   "gap": 0.4
  },
  {
   "v": "german",
   "t": "Ещё паштет из гусиных мозгов.",
   "gap": 0.55
  },
  {
   "v": "narrator",
   "t": "'Also pâté made from goose brains.' The preposition 'out of/from' plus the genitive plural describes what a dish is made of.",
   "gap": 0.4
  },
  {
   "v": "german",
   "t": "И свежий мозговой коктейль.",
   "gap": 0.55
  },
  {
   "v": "narrator",
   "t": "'And a fresh brain smoothie.' A relational adjective built from 'brain' modifies the drink.",
   "gap": 0.4
  },
  {
   "v": "german",
   "t": "Сеня, подай мне большой нож.",
   "gap": 0.55
  },
  {
   "v": "narrator",
   "t": "'Senya, hand me the big knife.' German smiles chillingly as he asks his zombie sous-chef for a knife.",
   "gap": 0.4
  },
  {
   "v": "anya",
   "t": "Да, весёлая у вас история.",
   "gap": 0.55
  },
  {
   "v": "narrator",
   "t": "'Yeah, that is quite a cheerful story you have.' Back in reality, Max reacts with dry irony to German's gruesome tale.",
   "gap": 0.4
  },
  {
   "v": "anya",
   "t": "Странный у нас коллектив получается.",
   "gap": 0.55
  },
  {
   "v": "narrator",
   "t": "'Our team turns out rather strange in it.' The reflexive verb means 'turns out' or 'comes out looking like'.",
   "gap": 0.4
  },
  {
   "v": "fedya",
   "t": "Совсем не смешное кино.",
   "gap": 0.55
  },
  {
   "v": "narrator",
   "t": "'Not a funny movie at all.' Fedya shudders at how everyone in German's story turned on one another.",
   "gap": 0.4
  },
  {
   "v": "anya",
   "t": "Давайте лучше дальше кокосы варить.",
   "gap": 0.55
  },
  {
   "v": "narrator",
   "t": "'Let's just go back to boiling coconuts instead.' Even boiling coconuts sounds better than German's zombie kitchen.",
   "gap": 0.4
  },
  {
   "v": "german",
   "t": "Работайте, не отвлекайтесь.",
   "gap": 0.55
  },
  {
   "v": "narrator",
   "t": "'Get to work, do not get distracted.' German walks off pleased with the impression he made. Now listen to the whole scene again at natural speed.",
   "gap": 0.9
  },
